@using TfLens.Core.AppManager
@using TrBlazeUI.Components.PasswordStrength

@*
    The password strength meter used by Register, Reset password and Profile.

    TR-003 is CLOSED. `docs/TfLens-UIDesign.md` §Library gaps always called for TrBlazeUI's
    `PasswordStrength`; TrBlazeUI.Components 2.0.0 did not ship it, so this file composed the meter
    from the library's own `Progress` — ONE bar — which is the fallback that same section named. The
    mockups do not draw one bar: `docs/mockups/register.html` draws `.pws` as FOUR segments over a
    two-word caption row, which is the shape 2.1.0-ci.10's `PasswordStrength` renders. The shim is
    gone and the real control is here.

    This wrapper stays rather than the pages calling `PasswordStrength` directly, and it earns its
    keep twice: it is where `data-testid="password-strength"` is anchored for the three screens that
    show a meter (Register, Reset password, Profile — the tests and the render gate locate it by that
    id), and it is where AppManager's own minimum length is handed to the control, so the meter and
    `PasswordRules.Describe`'s hint below it cannot disagree about what "long enough" means.
*@

<PasswordStrength Value="@Password"
                  MinimumLength="@PasswordRules.MinimumLength"
                  data-testid="password-strength" />

@code {
    /// <summary>The password being measured; never logged and never echoed back to the page.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Password { get; set; }
}
